Results
- Full affected unit/integration/provider/CLI regression: 436 passed in 31.62s.
- Focused work-store/transport/budget regression after late-receipt, idempotency, cost-resolver, and reconciliation request-count hardening: 80 passed in 7.40s.
- The budget concurrency integration launches two worker processes with 20 distinct requests through a real local blocking HTTP stub and shared temporary SQLite ledger. It observes real overlap and enforces global <=4, each quota group <=2, and each route <=1.
- Late 2xx, recognized 401/429, and bare 503 responses after lease expiry retain the work attempt as uncertain, do not fall back, store the late receipt, release the network-concurrency slot, and keep unknown cost reserved so admission pauses. A timeout with no HTTP response remains outcome_uncertain and keeps its slot. Identical late-receipt replay is idempotent; a conflicting HTTP status is rejected.
- Resolver exceptions and invalid numeric measurements after HTTP 200 become unknown-cost outcomes: the answer remains available, the network slot is released, the reservation stays unsettled, and new admission pauses.
- Budget denial is proven to happen before synchronous HTTP POST; unknown costs pause new dispatch; failed attempts/fallbacks share the same ledger; policy version updates preserve spend; async transport settles the same ledger with a deterministic test-only resolver.
- Scoped Ruff and Black checks pass on the five touched Python source/test files. `git diff --check` passes; Git emitted only existing LF/CRLF normalization warnings.

Independent review
- First Q09 snapshot review found one P2: a late definite HTTP response could strand an in-flight budget slot. The change was made with an atomic work-receipt/budget transaction and covered by regression tests.
- Follow-up hardening makes identical late receipts idempotent while rejecting conflicting status/cost/source; provider resolver exceptions and invalid measurements fail closed as unpriced after releasing a definitively ended HTTP concurrency slot. Reconciliation replay now rejects `confirmed_not_sent`/`completed` flips that would otherwise undercount request_counted, with zero-cost regression cases.
- Review also highlighted the duplicate late-receipt consistency boundary and cost-resolver failures after HTTP completion; exact replay is idempotent, conflicting outcomes are rejected, and invalid/failed cost resolution retains an unpriced reservation while closing the network slot.
- Final independent read-only review of the updated hashes is pending. Do not mark Q09 verified until it returns and remaining Q09 production fee-resolution/runner wiring is complete.
